      "source": [
        "### Exercise C.3 – Semantic search"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 15,
      "id": "f1c8b1db",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f1c8b1db",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "25c18824-0f4b-4c2b-955b-2a0fa3d0a7c9"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Query: 'medical treatment and doctor options'\n",
            "\n",
            "  score 0.539 | sci.med\n",
            "     I would say there are also significant numbers of unscrupulous doctors (of the squeaky-clean, traditional crew-cut, talk to the AMA before starting\n",
            "\n",
            "  score 0.533 | sci.med\n",
            "   Herman, I would think you of all people would/could distinguish between \"health\" and \"treatment of disease.\" All the prevention medicine people preac\n",
            "\n",
            "  score 0.353 | sci.med\n",
            "   It also gave me lots of problems with joint and muscle pain.  Seemed to trigger arthritis-like problems.  Sue\n",
            "\n",
            "  score 0.353 | sci.med\n",
            "   Who knows in this legal climate, but there is tremendous legal precendent for forcibly quarantining TB patients in sanitariums.  100 yrs ago it was d\n",
            "\n",
            "  score 0.259 | sci.med\n",
            "      Newsgroups: sci.med    Path: news.larc.nasa.gov!saimiri.primate.wisc.edu!zaphod.mps.ohio-state.edu!uwm.edu!cs.utexas.edu!uunet!think.com!hsdndev!s\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def semantic_search(query, documents, doc_embeddings, model, top_k=5):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return the top_k (index, score) pairs of the documents closest to the query.\"\"\"\n",
        "    # 1. encode the query\n",
        "    query_embedding = model.encode([query])\n",
        "    # 2. cosine similarity with every document embedding\n",
        "    similarities = cosine_similarity(query_embedding, doc_embeddings)[0]\n",
        "    # 3. indices of the top_k highest scores\n",
        "    top_indices = np.argsort(similarities)[::-1][:top_k]\n",
        "    return [(idx, similarities[idx]) for idx in top_indices]\n",
        "\n",
        "my_query = \"medical treatment and doctor options\"  # A query related to the sci.med category\n",
        "\n",
        "results = semantic_search(my_query, sampled_docs, doc_embeddings, sentence_model, top_k=5)\n",
        "assert len(results) == 5 and all(0 <= i < 30 for i, _ in results)\n",
        "print(f\"Query: '{my_query}'\")\n",
        "for idx, score in results:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n  score {score:.3f} | {sampled_labels[idx]}\")\n",
        "    print(\"  \" + sampled_docs[idx][:150].replace(\"\\n\", \" \"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "00b768fb",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "00b768fb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question C.4 (written)\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Are the results relevant to the query?\n",
        "2. Do they come from the expected category?\n",
        "3. Try a query that could match two of your categories: what happens?"
      ]
    },
