      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "61a06ebe",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "61a06ebe"
      },
      "source": [
        "<!-- ANSWER lab3.2-C4 -->\n",
        "**Your answer:**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Are the results relevant to the query?**\n",
        "   - Yes, they are highly relevant. The top-ranked results directly discuss medical professionals (\"doctors\"), treatments, disease management, and specific health symptoms (like joint and muscle pain).\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Do they come from the expected category?**\n",
        "   - Yes, all the top matches originate from the expected **`sci.med`** category. The transformer model correctly matched the semantic concept of \"medical treatment and doctor options\" to medical forum posts, even when exact keyword matches differed.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Try a query that could match two of your categories (e.g., \"computer graphics simulation of medical surgery\" or \"satellite imaging software\"): what happens?**\n",
        "   - When executing a query that bridges two categories (such as space/medical or graphics/medical), the model returns a blended list of results from both categories. The ranking is determined by which aspect of the query is prioritized by the sentence-embedding representation (e.g., matching a mix of `comp.graphics` and `sci.med` posts depending on individual document relevance).\n",
        "<!-- END ANSWER -->"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8a9815ad",
